      {
        "id": 127009,
        "name": "waedens",
        "username": "waedens",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/w/b3f665/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-21T02:35:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>There is one thing to keep in mind. The sentinels of the multiverse is the engine that keeps the company going. It keeps the lights on and doors open. Now they have started to diversify into things like distribution, which is a good thing, but it will be a sad day in my book when distribution is their main focus. What I am hoping is that they will use the core mechanic and continue to play with it. I liked GSF, but it doesn't get as much play time at my house simply because there is a lot of phases and accounting that needs doing and it gets to be too much for my kids. \"Play, Power, Draw\" is simple enough to do and I can help with the accounting and Bam! Like magic the multiverse comes alive. I could totally see a Wild West version of the game using the mechanics. A space version using the GSF universe would be totally awesome. It is my truest hope that they will keep the multiverse going. It has created some of our best holiday moments and it will be part of my children's holiday memories for the rest of their lives. Framed sentinels art prints are the decoration of choice in my kids room and I am super excited that our collection will be growing!</p><p>Okay, I am not sure where this post was going, but it sort of turned into a sentinels love letter. I will sign off now...</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
